  "step_3": "The decision reason requires adjusting probabilities below 20% by adding 10 percentage points and then computing a weighted sum. However, in this case, no outcome has a probability below 20%, so no adjustment occurs, and the reason reduces to comparing expected values. The individual does not refer to expected values, probability adjustments, or any weighted sum calculation. Instead, their reasoning is based on a qualitative trade-off between a small reduction in probability and a relatively large increase in payout. They do not mention probability weighting or any formal calculation. Therefore, the information considered by the individual (probability difference and outcome difference) does not align with the mechanism of the decision reason, and the justification does not match the rule of the reason. The individual did not use the decision reason to make the choice.",
